{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:09:24Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 81, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "40:i.e. `pending` is an array of full task objects (oldest pending-delete\n41:first, matching insertion order \u2014 no reordering logic needed). `UndoToast`\n49:It's positioned with `position: fixed`, so DOM order doesn't affect visual\n50:placement, but it does fix tab order: keyboard users reach the Undo\n80:Stacked in a column, oldest on top, each with its own independent bar:\n116:  border, white text (see contrast computation below).\n152:| Row gap (stacked toasts) | `0.5rem` | Matches `.task-list`'s existing `gap: 0.5rem` (`App.css:25`). |\n154:| Undo button border | `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)` | See contrast computation below. |\n157:| `z-index` | `10` | Nothing else in the app sets `z-index`; this is the first fixed/overlaid element, so any value above the default stacking order works \u2014 picked `10` with room to spare rather than `1`. |\n167:**Contrast \u2014 non-text (button border).** Border `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)`\n191:Undo by tabbing to it in DOM order (last, after all task rows) within the\n213:| 5 (two independent pending deletes) | \"Populated \u2014 many\" stacked state, independent per-row bars |", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LWr2n5rHQmGfGSGmWh2z5D", "session_id": "654814c6-720b-4415-b6c7-fe9892cf255f"}}
