function. React (especially under `StrictMode`, which `main.jsx:6` enables) may invoke updaters more than once to surface impurities; here it's harmless since `clearTimeout` on an already-cleared/`undefined` handle is a no-op, but it's worth moving the `clearTimeout` call outside the updater (read `pendingDeletes.get(id)` from render scope, or use a ref) if this pattern gets reused elsewhere.\n\nVERDICT: changes-requested", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "654814c6-720b-4415-b6c7-fe9892cf255f", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 1.0142280000000001}}
